[{"id":"VRCE-3-50-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":1,"english":"Her eyes expressing rage, weeping and fright, Sītā, as she was being carried away, weeping piteously, spoke to the grim-eyed lord of the Raksasas.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.477,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-53-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ff580db35cc2e709c8428524c356731b211dd67be3e663e0b5cb244e76fb20cd","compact":"bbd1efeb821eb51a5ebf9e24ec9d5c60e074c55bf09d157aed7c127f6418e151","nasal":"3485881cf433677fbed5d44620ea80e3865598af08238bd8773ea92ba402e264"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":2,"english":"Beholding the king of vultures slain by Rāvana, that one possessed of a face fair as the moon, stricken with grief, broke out into lamentations.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0d51dc800154a00f07e0bd06a8a76bc8b3a9d90f7549b359c522b0a8f19b1142","compact":"d3f7f93b6902efb15b2ac52256597dd95eba92ac651057264a58bcdfdfedc04e","nasal":"d3f7f93b6902efb15b2ac52256597dd95eba92ac651057264a58bcdfdfedc04e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":3,"english":"Throbbings of the eyes or other parts of the body, dreams, seeing birds or hearing their voice, are found to augur happiness or misery to men.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.661,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"42f84c76e9a0b549b6fcc9a7ab2e5c85a877b788af686ea919161a358f83c39e","compact":"87da0baa7922c4fb530dced023bb85946f99060199b70adebc124e5d48444449","nasal":"87da0baa7922c4fb530dced023bb85946f99060199b70adebc124e5d48444449"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-4","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":4,"english":"And, O Rāma, although birds and beasts are scampering away before you on my account, you under-stand not the mighty mishap that has befallen you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050004","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dcad8a1c7d3a3c206b4ff914a1ed51c562875a61b6f3d8c948bb597a5240e912","compact":"6dd23f536c8be61d52ea28a65c7ba49f9f1909db1bf51238d078c1ac262db1c7","nasal":"de98cc7c19b78da853495eef7addb58618d952b7f323a87596a1370263d1966a"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-5","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":5,"english":"O Kākutstha, O Laksmana, save me! Thus did that best of females, afflicted with fear, bewail; and those near (her) heard her lamentations.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050005","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"612ef42f8a52ca957320a00c677f2cb88ae31ab07a6318452b32239174f3483c","compact":"1d1ef7b257f9e177e9afcb18034b5bcae7310c20d3c122d44f0bc2df8e76b08e","nasal":"37bc03f1f40833f166ffa78c1648c44f7bb02835fea672cd88754497ae279a71"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-6","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":6,"english":"Thereat, that lord of the Rākşasas, Rāvana, darted towards Vaidehi, who, with a faded wreath for her ornament, was bewailing in forlorn guise.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2ce587256f0defb6db3b02343f6252c6a129cffad08136cdfe4fbbd365c54afc","compact":"7853721c5bd318bfee33f49c248e49707c16a2fb97f636a2211becb6c679adb1","nasal":"4f044666babbff001c10e69e0be3a87266780aa40268e4a4fbeb3c857991cb68"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":7,"english":"Exclaiming repeatedly, Leave off! Leave off, the lord of the Rākşasas got at her, as she was clasping a mighty trees as if it were a creeper.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.843,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b08dc34996227900f18cad59768ed8f6690790e799be5edfa00ae0e1144e8dfc","compact":"fbc587eb084201170ced11e964f4169b2485c9e22e5e5956a1fef79f4f5db6b9","nasal":"234619cdc344e4125d9b9cf832c1bbae219c67c9b5572c027e92175c34992f14"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":8,"english":"And as she, bereft of the company of Răma in the wilderness, was wailing, saying, O Rāma, O Rāma, that one resembling the Destroyer himself, with the view of compassing his own end, seized her by her hair. On Vaidehi being thus outraged, this entire world consisting of mobile and immobile objects, had its nature altered. A dense darkness enveloped (everything).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8104248e73cbe874d527abfab7343a2b1d754a2474136b8cafb1a8ed1e648da4","compact":"633a1f91ba6d7b393a75c311272e73d8769f68817e8aed21b5b8591b4e9e418c","nasal":"2650d3add0a937922b548c064225247a7467915eecc2cfbaa30832756808f127"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":9,"english":"And as she, bereft of the company of Răma in the wilderness, was wailing, saying, O Rāma, O Rāma, that one resembling the Destroyer himself, with the view of compassing his own end, seized her by her hair. On Vaidehi being thus outraged, this entire world consisting of mobile and immobile objects, had its nature altered. A dense darkness enveloped (everything).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f3671d066fd125e9a6f224f6661dffe0e2749fbada6f0ffdf0e695fed77e1234","compact":"9e2912203c7478733ac76f5057102af008659cbe05b704fa6e2cd55a351f2f4b","nasal":"a30a0ef927189a1a8661e3f9f0cb24840cf5dc8ecf5a045658bfe34307413a58"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":10,"english":"And the air did not breathe there; and the sun grew dim. Espying with his divine vision that Sītā was overcome, that Deity, the graceful Great-father exclaimed, Our work is accomplished.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.845,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3ed8e11e4a200bcae22e59ca5d5696f1cdb49a4dacaa19356e50c0ae0bcdd029","compact":"38ef8f2736a5459bae8f42611d76205a8c531692d325f1d48c89c7a614488444","nasal":"38ef8f2736a5459bae8f42611d76205a8c531692d325f1d48c89c7a614488444"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":11,"english":"And the air did not breathe there; and the sun grew dim. Espying with his divine vision that Sītā was overcome, that Deity, the graceful Great-father exclaimed, Our work is accomplished. And seeing Sītā overpowered, the supreme saints inhabiting the Dandaka forest, concluding the destruction of Rāvaņa to be as good as accomplished without much ado, became at once delighted and aggrieved.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.929,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-9","DUTT-3-52-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1852fae1bf1b3fb62f82e39615443987672db9ef2aef3f8e1d62aaef1fdb67f4","compact":"fdec412e19e81e435192f7676ee1af799962ea2bd0b913bfef5e257522468cd5","nasal":"b2698297b835551a686513ce2a8fe8e542cab5e8cf166b4ec590f7eb3bb97440"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":12,"english":"As she went on weeping with ( Rāma, O Lakşmaņa, Rāvana-lord of Rākşasas—taking her, coursed through the sky.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.429,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e3412fff5de0e349b2ed8c9a80aa0a2a4878965bf4d11b1af219e5088d3544b9","compact":"797136d573b02a19553b0cf18ea462508ce5fc33acd862cbc5032dea845f505b","nasal":"a21e3031ee6489ed1cc2a75c3e6309824c0f5b5730b39c4be959cf08dcc04b26"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":13,"english":"And then the king's daughter hued like molten gold, clad in a yellow silken cloth, looked exceedingly beautiful like to lighting.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.679,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9266c60a2a656d8059619609f4e303f683a85dc7f2ee9a74f6ec64578c769add","compact":"83550998b33ba1fd6ef991cf593cddc1c8b3ff8e35a1886542e323fff40e3660","nasal":"f6c6bedc79cef4624f5f8f9c6dcbfbfffc730b2ab1daa7675d67dfb2d720f8c6"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-14","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":14,"english":"And on her yellow cloth streaming up, Rāvaņa looked surpassingly graceful like a hill aflame with fire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.793,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a7145cdb612e041e74c070dc4499851ddbde6f7fc966da47dab071749a6dad41","compact":"a3e130ba55c78e11e7f60a6ab6a7ab4f08e5d8c28bf33814ac18c76c4e2b62ce","nasal":"a3e130ba55c78e11e7f60a6ab6a7ab4f08e5d8c28bf33814ac18c76c4e2b62ce"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-15","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":15,"english":"And coppery fragrant lotus-leaves belonging to the eminently auspicious Vaidehī showered upon Ravana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050015","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"89ccab8bd6da04caa90c75425fedbda54203de8b2242b5d1a059ce1b9cb5c0d3","compact":"83b23f09ec567caf22048b1d7634a99f22bd4eb873a7e82522bd9dbb3de482b0","nasal":"1776d5ecd686c3d781e6b5ff4a942633b4280782a4fdd9815b173c3f35202a75"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-16","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":16,"english":"And her gold-glowing silken cloth, flying in the air, appeared like clouds coloured by the sunken sun.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050016","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cbac4f24010b4def24c50bfce9af883431d3a4affebef7011a933c1dc44bf5f5","compact":"eb42cbd8507d8c92e536c001c99c093c0dab970a250b4e6da5bb278489d13aa8","nasal":"3ae58c217b667958f989b829c22811616125db56c31c6c96445496c18d09be49"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-17","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":17,"english":"And her blameless countenance on Rāvana's lap in the sky did not appear beauteous without Rāma, like a lotus without its stalk; It appeared like the moon risen tearing away dark clouds. And in the aerial regions her countenance on Rāvana's lap furnished with a fair forehead and graceful hair glowing like the interior of a lotus, without scars, graced with white, shining, stainless teeth, having excellent eyes, lovely like the moon, having a shapely nose, a rubeous upper lip, wearing the splendour of gold in the sky, that captivating countenance of hers in consequence of her weeping, and of being stained with tears, as also owing to the violence it had undergone at the hands of the lord of Rākşasas,-did not appear beautiful without Rāma' like the moon risen during the day.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-16","DUTT-3-52-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5f0d023eac0c0399df994530092a4af82056350f6988292caaddbcc54d78eee3","compact":"fb09fc008f76183e540ab76aef732a2adc26d13943aec75f4f0ae1906e2d9775","nasal":"87f61da6862134b773a0fc1c985cd6aa5960b1a3dc605328e76545b9a0dad5dc"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-18","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":18,"english":"It appeared like the moon risen tearing away dark clouds. And in the aerial regions her countenance on Rāvana's lap furnished with a fair forehead and graceful hair glowing like the interior of a lotus, without scars, graced with white, shining, stainless teeth, having excellent eyes, lovely like the moon, having a shapely nose, a rubeous upper lip, wearing the splendour of gold in the sky, that captivating countenance of hers in consequence of her weeping, and of being stained with tears, as also owing to the violence it had undergone at the hands of the lord of Rākşasas,-did not appear beautiful without Rāma' like the moon risen during the day.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050018","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fcf18feccdba5f2a4cc0c984f4946821616f2b3291999b516138522ecb594659","compact":"f1885e6c723f2335f98ff636cabc2bd81054064b939bf1a9b82936dda1539399","nasal":"4b3c0225ad017bd5fc741eacb0f938aa75ea2c2305d19a379db5703688cb2ae3"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-19","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":19,"english":"It appeared like the moon risen tearing away dark clouds. And in the aerial regions her countenance on Rāvana's lap furnished with a fair forehead and graceful hair glowing like the interior of a lotus, without scars, graced with white, shining, stainless teeth, having excellent eyes, lovely like the moon, having a shapely nose, a rubeous upper lip, wearing the splendour of gold in the sky, that captivating countenance of hers in consequence of her weeping, and of being stained with tears, as also owing to the violence it had undergone at the hands of the lord of Rākşasas,-did not appear beautiful without Rāma' like the moon risen during the day.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.662,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-52-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3050019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e14fb0df47aa184d4fe795287753f614fdbb86400bfa4161a6d963ec7dcf4e56","compact":"8098471e5933f8d05c16abf77a6bf98551ad6ff6eb9f16afbc26845929ec1276","nasal":"454edcad06c167dc6d63d926063493fe0867802b9568f58921ccc12cd8e991a6"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-50-20","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":50,"verse":20,"english":"It appeared like the moon risen tearing away dark clouds. And in the aerial regions her countena